  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rambali vs State Of U.P. & Anr. on 8 October, 2020 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Court No. - 8 Case :- U/S 482/378/407 No. - 2219 of 2020 Applicant :- Rambali Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. & Anr. Counsel for Applicant :- Sunil Kumar Singh,Vivek Kumar Divedi Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Virendra Kumar-II,J.",
    "facts": "A complaint has been filed by the Food Safety Officer, in which it is narrated that on 02.05.2017 at about 4:20 p.m. in Jassapurwa, District Hardoi the Food Safety Officer inspected the premises/ shop of the petitioner and took samples of ice candy liquid, which was sent for chemical analysis to the Public Analyst, U.P., Agra which was found to be substandard and unsafe as per Section 3(1)(zzz)(v) of F.S.S. Act, 2006. Saccharine sodium was present in the sample. On the basis of complaint filed by the Food Safety Officer the trial court has summoned the petitioner vide impugned order dated 24.01.2020. Learned A.G.A. has submitted that Food Safety Officer, after inspection of premises/ shop of petitioner found that ice candy liquid was found substandard as per the report of Public Analyst, therefore, proceedings of complaint case are not liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner has submitted that the Food Safety Officer has filed a false complaint against the petitioner and no opportunity was given to the petitioner to contradict the report submitted by the Public Analyst of the Laboratory at Agra.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner has submitted that the Food Safety Officer has filed a false complaint against the petitioner and no opportunity was given to the petitioner to contradict the report submitted by the Public Analyst of the Laboratory at Agra.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
